  "youtube": {
    "title": "Stuck? Stop Sitting There. #shorts",
    "description": "Staring at a blank page, forcing ideas that won't come? Your body might be the problem, not your brain.\n\nIn Stanford experiments, people came up with about 60% more creative ideas while walking than while sitting. Walking indoors on a treadmill worked as well as walking outside, and the boost lasted for a while after they sat back down. It helps with brainstorming, not with single right-answer problems.\n\nNext time you're stuck: 10 minutes, no phone, just walk.\n\nResearch: Oppezzo & Schwartz (2014), \"Give Your Ideas Some Legs\", Journal of Experimental Psychology: Learning, Memory, and Cognition.\n\n#shorts #creativity #psychology #productivity #study #animation #selfimprovement",
